  "name": "gardner in rounds with meek pawns",
  "description": "Gardner's minichess played in rounds, as in gardner in rounds, with one change: a pawn wins no collision. When a pawn and another piece step onto the same square in the same round, the other piece stands there and the pawn is removed (in gardner in rounds both are removed); two pawns meeting are both removed, as before. A pawn still captures a piece that stands still exactly as before. So a cheap pawn can no longer trade itself for a queen by guessing where the queen will step, and the dear pieces may go where pawns could follow.",
